    ],
    "justification": "A fully enumerable dense design fixes the sign, normalization, and magnitude of the projection correction.",
    "gap": "No cited random-group inference result reports this finite dense witness or the factor-two CR2 excess.",
    "consumer": "The witness is a regression test for symbolic derivations and for a design-aware \\({\\tt vcovCR}\\) diagnostic.",
    "proof_tex": "For a pair \\(A=\\{j,k\\}\\), write \\(h(A)=(a_j+a_k)/2\\).  Among the \\(\\binom82=28\\) pairs, six have value \\(1\\), six have value \\(-1\\), and sixteen have value zero.  Thus \\(\\mathbb E_8h=0\\) and\n\\[\n V_{1,n}=\\mathbb E_8h^2=\\frac{12}{28}=\\frac37.\n\\]\nMoreover \\(h(A)=2^{-1}\\sum_{i\\in A}a_i\\) is degree one: averaging it over a disjoint pair gives\n\\[\n (\\mathsf K_8h)(A)=\\frac1{6}\\sum_{i\\notin A}a_i\n =-\\frac1{6}\\sum_{i\\in A}a_i=-\\frac13h(A).\n\\]\nThus \\(E_{\\tau,1,n}=\\|h\\|_8^2=3/7\\).  Theorem~\\ref{thm:exact-kneser-identity} gives \\(C_{11,n}=(-1/3)(3/7)=-1/7\\), while all control quantities vanish.  Since \\(p_n=1/2\\), Theorem~\\ref{thm:exact-pame-variance} gives\n\\[\n \\sigma_n^2=\\frac{(3/7)/(1/2)}4-\\frac17-\\frac{-1/7}{2}=\\frac17\n\\]\nand\n\\[\n \\mathbb E\\widehat V_{\\mathrm{CR2},n}\n =\\frac{V_{1,n}-C_{11,n}}{G_{1n}}\n =\\frac{3/7+1/7}{2}=\\frac27.\n\\]\nThere are \\((8-1)!!=105\\) perfect matchings and \\(\\binom42=6\\) treated-pair choices per matching.  Directly summing \\(\\widehat\\tau_n^2\\) and \\(\\widehat V_{\\mathrm{CR2},n}\\) over these \\(630\\) equally likely points gives respectively \\(630/7\\) and \\(1260/7\\); division by \\(630\\) reproduces \\(1/7\\) and \\(2/7\\).  The estimator mean is zero by sign balance (or by Theorem~\\ref{thm:exact-pame-variance}), so the first moment calculation is the variance.",
